  "varnames": [],
  "consts": [
   "core/matrix_synth.py - V2.0.2: code-side synthesis of MATRIX grid recipes.\n\nWhy this module exists\n----------------------\n``core/recipe_synth.py`` synthesizes a ``line_pattern`` for LINE-ITEM layouts from\nthe AI's verbatim sample rows, then proves it by offline replay. Grid layouts\n(COLIN'S / SAKHA / NEW YORKER) had no such path: the AI cannot usefully quote a\n2-D grid row by row, so V2.0.0/V2.0.1 fell back to a SECOND AI call\n(``core/ai/recipe_infer.py``) plus a manual confirmation dialog. That second call\nis the slowest and most failure-prone step in the pipeline (it is what made\nOM-907398 fail outright in V2.0.0).\n\nThe key realisation is that a grid does not need to be *read* by a model at all -\nit needs to be *located*. And a real order grid announces itself structurally:\n\n    * a SIZE HEADER line: a run of size-like tokens ending in a TOTAL token;\n    * DATA ROWS underneath whose printed ROW TOTAL lands, by x-position, exactly\n      in that TOTAL column.\n\nLook-alike tables (assortment-ratio grids, pack break-ups, SUMMARY/GENERAL TOTAL\nrestatements) either miss the second property or sit under their own distinct\nheader, so they can be told apart without reading a single word.\n\nSo this module:\n\n    1. finds every candidate grid in the document (purely structural);\n    2. derives the anchors around it (destination split, section, summary,\n       colour block, colour-code shape) as a small ORDERED candidate set;\n    3. replays each candidate recipe offline with ``registry.parse`` and keeps the\n       FIRST one that reproduces the AI-reported totals exactly.\n\nStep 3 is the same gate ``recipe_synth.verify_recipe`` applies to line items, so a\nmatrix recipe reaching the cache has been proven against the printed totals - no\nsecond AI call, no manual dialog. When nothing verifies we raise and the caller\nfalls back to the legacy inference path exactly as before.\n\nNo customer name is hardcoded anywhere.\n",
